# Packages installed into the LIVE ISO itself -- the environment the installer
# runs in, NOT the system it installs.
#
# Three lists, three different questions, and mixing them up is how the bug
# this file exists to fix happened in the first place:
#
#   deck-install.packages   pacstrapped onto the TARGET at install time
#   deck-mirror.packages    carried in the offline mirror for later
#   deck-live.packages      installed into the LIVE root -- this file
#
# builder/build-iso.sh (patched by iso/overlay/patches/deck-packages.patch,
# seam S6) appends every entry here to `packages.x86_64`, which is both what
# mkarchiso pacstraps into the live root AND one of the inputs to the offline
# mirror's download list. So an entry here is downloaded once and installed
# once, into the ISO.
#
# ⚠️ Entries must be BARE names, never repo-qualified. Unlike
# deck-mirror.packages this list is resolved against the offline mirror by
# mkarchiso as well as against the online repos, and a qualified name aborts
# the single-repo offline resolve.
#
# 🔴 iso/bin/build guard 6.7 reads this file before Docker starts and refuses
# a build whose live ISO would carry the on-screen keyboard's script without
# the library it imports. Do not remove an entry to "slim the ISO" without
# reading that guard.

# --- the on-screen keyboard's runtime dependency ----------------------------
#
# /usr/local/bin/deck-input-mapper does `from evdev import InputDevice, UInput,
# ecodes, list_devices` at module scope (src/deck-input-mapper.py), and so does
# the layout core it imports (src/deck_osk_layout.py, for `ecodes`). Without
# this package the mapper dies at its first import line, deck-form.sh's
# deck_form_text_prompt never sees the `deck-input-mapper: bound` marker, and
# every text screen -- Wi-Fi password, username, account password, hostname --
# comes up with no way to type on a machine that has no keyboard.
#
# That is exactly what shipped in omarchy-2026.08.15-x86_64-quattro.iso and was
# found on the first real-hardware boot:
# docs/findings/P32-osk-mapper-missing-from-live-iso.md.
#
# extra/python-evdev, BSD-3-Clause (redistributable -- CLAUDE.md's "nothing
# unlicensed or AUR-only"), depends only on glibc and python, both already in
# the live root. Measured 2026-08-15: 123.70 KiB download, 830.98 KiB installed.
python-evdev
